{
  "paraphrase": "The unconventional royal wedding took place on Saturday when Norway's Princess Märtha Louise, who claims psychic abilities, married Durek Verrett, a Californian who identifies as a hereditary shaman. Despite the unusual nature of the union, crowds gathered along the cloudy streets of Geiranger hoping to see the royal bride. The 52-year-old princess, who ranks fourth in succession to Norway's throne as the sole daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, wed 49-year-old Verrett in a Church of Norway service at the Hotel Union, a four-star establishment in a village near the Geiranger fjord. Among the wedding party were seven bridesmaids, including the princess's teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her previous marriage to deceased Norwegian writer Ari Behn, which ended in 2017. The ceremony drew approximately 350 guests, featuring Norwegian Crown Prince Haakon with Crown Princess Mette-Marit, Swedish royals Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel, plus Dutch royals Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien. The princess has pursued an unconventional path, having claimed supernatural communication abilities and operated a spiritual healing academy for ten years where she instructed students in angelic communication. In 2022, she relinquished her formal royal responsibilities to concentrate on commercial ventures with Verrett while creating clearer boundaries between personal enterprises and Norway's monarchy. Verrett presents himself on social media as divinely inspired and an 'energy activator,' counting among his high-profile clientele Gwyneth Paltrow, the Goop entrepreneur he refers to as his 'soul sister.'"
}
```

